# Fleet Builder Resume Prompt
File: openOODA/scripts/fleet/prompts/resume.oot

Provenance: converted from openOODA/scripts/fleet/prompts/resume.md (9 lines). The resume
line, the git safety rule, and the extra note slot are preserved. The page rule, the gate
sequence, the prove list, and the report format were added to match the sibling prompts in
this directory. The WIP branch namespace is the generic `wip/fleet-<host>-<pane>` form.

{{RESUME_LINE}}
The git safety rule still applies:

  - commit and push every finished file to
    git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/wip/fleet-$(hostname -s)-{{PANE}}
  - push to master/main only after `make verify test` has passed twice
  - never leave a repo dirty for more than one step
  - never use `git add -A` or `git add .`; stage explicit paths only
  - never publish an internal node name or a `100.x.x.x` address in a published file

BEFORE YOU EDIT
  - stay in the repo of the resumed task; do not start a new work item
  - read AGENTS.md in the repo root and follow it
  - keep every page inside the Page Rule: 16-256 lines per file, <=8 functions per page,
    <=40 lines per function, <=8 pages per directory, and the 4-element Academy header
  - run /home/ubermetroid/.local/bin/lint-oo-size and get 0 violations

GATE (in this order, before you report done)
  - export OODA_COMPILER=/Projects/openOODA-core/oodac/bin/oodac.real
  - export OODA_NO_JAIL=1
  - export OO_LIST_AMBIENT_QUOTA=8589934592
  - make verify && make test      # TWICE, byte-identical post-build output
  - diff the post-build output of run 1 and run 2 and show the result

PROVE before you report done
  - git status -s                  -> empty
  - git rev-parse HEAD             -> equals origin/master and origin/main
  - lint-oo-size                   -> 0 violations
  - make verify test               -> PASS twice, byte-identical output

REPORT a table: file -> change -> gate result.
If you must stop, state the exact blocker.
Do not ask for permission to proceed; only stop for a genuine ambiguity in the task itself.

{{EXTRA}}
